<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16779" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύμ-πτωτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not falling in, full,</i>
			of face or body, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Hum.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.25
			</span></i>, al.; <i>not closing,</i> of the edges of a wound, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χείλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antyll.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				7.11.10
			</span></i>; <i>not liable to collapse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.Lond.
				26.50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not touching,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ψυχῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> esp. in Math.,
			of lines or planes <i>which never meet,</i> e. g. parallel
			straight lines, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Deff.</i><i><span class="en">
				70
			</span></i>; of lines <i>which do not cut</i> a curve, <i>non-secant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῇ τομῇ αἱ ΓΔ, ΓΕ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollon.Perg.
					<u>Con.</u>
					2.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύμπτωτος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμμή</span>), ἡ,
				<i>asymptote,</i> of the hyperbola, ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.3
			</span></i>, etc.; of the conchoid, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Euc.</u>
				p.366
			</span></i> F.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
